<title>INDIA: Minister sees India self-sufficient in edible oil.</title>
<headline>Minister sees India self-sufficient in edible oil.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India, a net importer of edible oil, is likely to become self-sufficient in the commodity during the ninth five-year plan which began on April 1, 1997, Agriculture Minister Chaturanan Mishra said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;India should not only be self-sufficient in edible oil production but it should be able to export it,&quot; a government statement quoted Mishra as saying.</p>
<p>Mishra was speaking at a meeting of the state-run National Oilseeds and Vegetable Oils Development Board.</p>
<p>India at present imports more than one million tonnes of edible oil annually. Industry officials expect edible oil imports to grow to 1.5 million tonnes in 1996/97 (November-October) from 1.2 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Mishra said there was great scope for oil extraction from mango kernel. He also said about six percent of mustard oil was wasted during extraction due to a lack of advanced machinery.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
